        "thought_text": "Consider implementing a bucket sort approach to distribute the vectors into bins based on their polar angles. Each bin will contain vectors whose angles fall within a certain range. By comparing vectors within the same bin and those at the boundaries of adjacent bins, you can efficiently find the pair of vectors with the minimal non-oriented angle. This method reduces the number of direct angle comparisons needed, leading to improved performance for large inputs.",
